lines=['# Wave 02-03 acceptance reconciliation','',f"Reviewed all 24 assigned leaves: **{counts['complete']} complete, {counts['partial']} partial, {counts['blocked']} blocked**. Complete recommendations: A-M-24/31/32/33 and A-E-01/09/10. These are named architectural/component results; the 20 editor V leaves, broader editor trust/device/AT and production gates remain open.",'','## Evidence and attribution','',f"Modified dev HEAD `{e['head']}`; capture `{e['capturedAt']}`. [evidence.json](evidence.json) records {len(e.get('inputHashes'))} focused input hashes and {len(e.get('testDeclarations'))} unit/native test declarations. All fourteen assigned editor source/test/CSS directories match FA-02. The saved production graph has only the four coordinator picker/TextArea deltas listed in that file. Current imports were inspected for their domain boundary; no claim that old dist contains those fixes.",'','FA-04 Node 24 unit evidence is retained: its original overall check failed nine calendar cases, corrected in the affected rerun. The editor suites were among the passing unaffected suites. Existing package/foundation evidence and parallel-03 owned API review are reused without rerunning suites. Local analysis used Python 3.9.6 and Node 26.5.0 on macOS; no new supported-runtime result is claimed.','', 'F and T active files contain no open rows; individual family case mappings survive in next100-c21 through next100-c34 reports. Their older native holds for T-C25-02 and T-C34-10 are superseded by the later executed docs-owned fixture results in `backlog-execution-2026-10-15.md:17–64`. Historical Storybook evidence is retained separately, never represented as a docs-host execution.','', 'HB-14 supplies EditableTitleField presentation/RTL evidence; HB-18 supplies ColumnsLayoutModal, ImageUploadModal and LinkUrlModal. The accepted execution receipts describe actual native engines and reviewed screenshots. Their named ignored `packages/ui/artifacts/...` raw directories are absent locally, as explicitly tested in evidence.json. This report reuses the accepted receipts and current source/assertions; it does not claim fresh screenshot inspection or recover missing raw artifacts. Exact historical source/host/build limits remain those of each receipt (modified dev, including d3201f0-based batches), not this current HEAD.','', 'The [command and trust matrix](command-and-trust-matrix.md) is new review work: it enumerates retained positive evidence and missing acceptance deliverables instead of repeating blanket editor holds. Shared ledgers/counts were not edited.','']
